# Finite certificate for the outer M₁₂ overlap generator images

Each multiplication row packs 128 seven-bit entries into a natural number.
The word-induction check below reduces all products to generator edges, whose
permutation interpretation is proved in `Steps`. The inverse and order tables
are checked against these products. Ten order tests on a, b, c, ab, ac, bc,
aab, aac, abc, abcbc force the predicted inner/central images.

The explicit witnesses and packed rows are untrusted data. `Arithmetic` gives
their group interpretation, and `Coverage` applies the tests to automorphisms.
The source inputs and ATLAS attribution are inherited from `Data` and `Basic`;
source context is Aschbacher--Smith F.1.12(I)(13), pp.262–263, and 14.2.21, p.988.
-/
